# Generated artefacts - keep the folders, ignore everything produced into them.
# Git cannot track an empty directory, so a .gitkeep placeholder is committed
# in each and re-included by the negations below.
#
# Nothing in either folder is versioned. Everything there is reproducible:
#   model/   `python main.py train`    -> door_model.json, door_reference.json,
#                                         door_model.joblib, training_report.json
#   output/  `python main.py predict`  -> door_predictions.csv, door_detail.csv
#
# NOTE: `train` also needs Backend/02_Datasets/Door/Train.csv, which is ignored
# (provided hackathon material). A fresh clone therefore has the code but not
# the data, so it must obtain the dataset before it can regenerate the model,
# and predict.py will not run until it has. That is deliberate - generated data
# stays out of git - but it means the repo is not self-contained.
Backend/Door/model/*
Backend/Door/output/*
!Backend/Door/model/.gitkeep
!Backend/Door/output/.gitkeep

# Submission bundle - built from output/, never edited by hand
predictions.zip

# Frontend build artefacts, dependencies and local secrets
Frontend/node_modules/
Frontend/dist/
Frontend/.vite/
Frontend/.env*.local

# SHM: commit source and artifacts/model.json, not datasets or experiment output.
Backend/SHM/dataset_shm/
Backend/SHM/.cache/
Backend/SHM/outputs/
Backend/SHM/shm_predictions.csv
.pytest_cache/
